Research Software Engineering with Python — Irving and colleagues (@rc-rse: 0, is #book, #part-of @rc-sources) { r_07D4PDD4HGKNK3PW4M90YSV2QY
Damien Irving, Kate Hertweck, Luke Johnston, Joel Ostblom, Charlotte Wickham, and Greg Wilson. Research Software Engineering with Python: Building Software that Makes Research Possible. CRC Press/Taylor & Francis, 2021. ISBN 978-0-367-69834-8.

[Authors’ complete rendered book](https://third-bit.com/py-rse/) · [Authors’ source and edition information](https://github.com/merely-useful/py-rse).

Read the complete book in sequence after the early programming preparation, completing the exercises and following its substantial research-software project. It develops the shell, Python, version control, collaboration, Make workflows, configuration, testing, error handling, publishing, and packaging. Its introductory page explicitly assumes loops, conditionals, functions, and reading files; this trail introduces those before relying on that preparation.

The rendered 2021 edition states CC BY 4.0 for content and MIT for code, with attribution and component notices retained. The source repository directs readers to third-bit.com; an older merely-useful.tech address was not accessible during checking. Author, edition, full-book access, and licence statements checked on 29 October 2026. No book or companion corpus is copied into the repository.

**Return:** [Reproducible-computation sources — books, research, and primary manuals](../Sources.lingua#r_7RY36NATQ0VQE5JMJAMF6KXK3K).
